#: liminal-union/units/nations/drake/p0-saurian-brave.cfg:40
msgid "Saurian braves are very small of frame, and though they are somewhat frail because of this, they are very, very agile. In combat, their size allows them to dart past defenses that would hold any grown man at bay, making them a tricky foe to deal with."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Saurian_Elementalist, race=lizard, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/drake/p0-saurian-elementalist.cfg:4
msgid "Saurian Elementalist"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: liminal-union/units/nations/drake/p0-saurian-elementalist.cfg:21
#: liminal-union/units/nations/loyalist/mf0-initiate.cfg:24
#: liminal-union/units/nations/rebels/h0-elvish-healer.cfg:27
msgid "staff"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: liminal-union/units/nations/drake/p0-saurian-elementalist.cfg:30
msgid "curse"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Saurian_Elementalist, race=lizard, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/drake/p0-saurian-elementalist.cfg:43
msgid "Saurians have some knowledge of what men call sorcery, but their practice of it reeks of augury and black magic. It is little understood, but rightly regarded with fear by those against whom it is used."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Fellah, race=dunefolk, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-fellah.cfg:12
msgid "Dune Serf"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Fellah, race=dunefolk, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-fellah.cfg:27
msgid "A serf, is the backbone of the dunefolk economy, and a soldiers of last resort. While not warlike by nature, they can be forced to stubbornly fight because they fear the subduer's whip. However, if you’re hurling serfs at your foes, you’re clearly out of superior forces."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Muhandiz, race=dunefolk, gender=male,female
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-muhandiz.cfg:14
msgid "💥 Dune Dropout"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Muhandiz, race=dunefolk, gender=male,female
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-muhandiz.cfg:41
msgid "Unlike the learned herbalists, dunefolk dropouts have given up their life as undergraduates. These students develop an interest in alchemical substances and explosives in order to prove themselves useful in asymmetric war. That they will die in the process of obtaining 'victory' does not interest those who carry a suicide bomb into battle. The dunefolk officials promote self-sacrifice as an act of devotion and promise 'heavenly rewards' for killing 'infidels'. However, not few are forced into it by their clans as a repay of an honor debt, or by blackmail, because the demand for such bombers is always greater than the supply."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-muhandiz.cfg:60
msgid "bomb"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dune_Nagaling
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-nagaling.cfg:7
msgid "Nagaling"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-nagaling.cfg:25
#: liminal-union/units/nations/northerners/f0-naga-hooligan.cfg:25
msgid "chakri"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dune_Nagaling
#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Naga_Hooligan
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/f0-nagaling.cfg:34
#: liminal-union/units/nations/northerners/f0-naga-hooligan.cfg:34
msgid "A nagaling is a young Naga of the southern waters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dune_Horseman
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc0-dune-horseman.cfg:7
msgid "Dune Horseman"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc0-dune-horseman.cfg:16
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc1-herbalist.cfg:35
msgid "mace"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc0-dune-horseman.cfg:25
msgid "composite bow"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dune_Horseman
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc0-dune-horseman.cfg:34
msgid "Only the males of the dunefolk are allowed to ride horses on raids and in war. These young horsemen primarily function as scouts and messengers, or occasionally as supporting forces for weakened lines."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Herbalist, race=dunefolk
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc1-herbalist.cfg:8
msgid "Dune Herbalist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Herbalist, race=dunefolk
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc1-herbalist.cfg:25
msgid "As those responsible for caring for the ill and wounded among the Dunefolk, herbalists possess both the medicinal skills to heal a variety of afflictions and the skill to seek and gather restorative herbs. Their motivations are many; some look to it as an adventure or as a steady source of pay while others feel it to be a duty to their society. No matter the reason, these healers are an invaluable part of Dunefolk society and are especially useful for their ability to administer quick treatments in the midst of battle or while traveling in the desert. Even among the nomadic Dunefolk, herbalists journey a great deal in search of the various flora and fauna that supply their work. Hardened by their travels, many of these men are even able to heal themselves."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Hashishine, race=dunefolk, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc2-hashishine.cfg:13
msgid "Dune Hashishi"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Hashishine, race=dunefolk, gender=male
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc2-hashishine.cfg:43
msgid "Amongst the dunefolk developed a special unit, the Hashishi, the best assassinator. The Hashishi assailants are trained in techniques of hand-to-hand combat. Their most preferred weapon for a kill from behind are multiple knives dipped in poison. However, the Hashishi became best known for their excessive psychoactive drug abuse: hashish. The only downside of this practice in an army is, that by altering the visual, auditory, and olfactory senses, the drugs lead Hashishi sometimes to poison the false person, even merry comrades."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc2-hashishine.cfg:50
msgid "blade"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc2-hashishine.cfg:62
msgid "kick & punch"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: liminal-union/units/nations/dunefolk/sc2-hashishine.cfg:71
msgid "hashishi attack"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Miner, race=dwarf
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-miner.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Miner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Miner, race=dwarf
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-miner.cfg:18
msgid "Dwarvish miners are the grunt workers of Dwarvish society. They take the precious ores out of the ground, but do not ever take part in the crafting of weapons or artifacts."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade # pierce
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-miner.cfg:37
msgid "pick"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Pilferer, race=human, gender=male,female
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-pilferer.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Pilferer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Pilferer, race=human, gender=male,female
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-pilferer.cfg:19
msgid "Pilferers are impoverished individuals who can be found in the back alleys of any town. They subsist by petty crime and day labor, and even rats are always a welcome meal in such conditions."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-pilferer.cfg:51
msgid "female^Pilferer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Woodcutter, race=dwarf
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-woodcutter.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Woodcutter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Dwarvish_Woodcutter, race=dwarf
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-woodcutter.cfg:18
msgid "For dwarves, lumber is irreplacable in its function as fuel and construction material. Woodcutters are responsible for retrieving it from the forests of the overworld."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-dwarvish-woodcutter.cfg:23
msgid "axe"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Gryphon
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-gryphon.cfg:7
msgid "Gryphon Hatchling"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-gryphon.cfg:16
#: liminal-union/units/nations/undead/sc0-ghouling.cfg:19
msgid "claws"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Gryphon
#: liminal-union/units/nations/knalgan/f0-gryphon.cfg:25
msgid "Dwarves train young domesticated gryphon hatchlings. These majestic creatures will be masters of the sky. Gryphon hatchlings serve as scouts for their dwarvish owners."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Nobleman, race=human
#: liminal-union/units/nations/loyalist/f0-loyalist-nobleman.cfg:5
msgid "Nobleman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=LIUN_Nobleman, race=human
#: liminal-union/units/nations/loyalist/f0-loyalist-nobleman.cfg:19
msgid "Noblemen lead a life of relative luxury and do not shy away to show this to the world. The privilege to carry weapons and their choreographic movements have attracted quite a number of looks from court ladies."
msgstr ""

